# Archive safety

The live archive is the only copy of data its sources already deleted. Treat it as production.

- The live database changes only through a release (`bun run release`, see release-route.mdc).
- Evaluate retrieval on the live archive, read-only: the installed `memindex` CLI (`sql`, recipes,
  `--search`) or SELECT/EXPLAIN. Real usage, sizes and signal come from it. Ranking changes are still
  gated on the snapshot, because the live archive moves and contains the eval chats themselves.
- Tests (`bun test`) run only on the Supabase test stack (`memindex-dev`, port 54422): they wipe and
  reset it. Stop it when idle with `supabase stop` (data kept); tests need it running.
- Dev builds (`bun apps/memindex/src/cli.ts …`) run only against the eval snapshot or a scratch
  database, never the configured store.
- Point the CLI elsewhere per command, never by exporting:
  `MEMINDEX_STORE=postgresql://…/memindex_snapshot bun apps/memindex/src/cli.ts sql …`.
  An exported `MEMINDEX_STORE` outlives the command, and `memindex install --yes` saves it as the
  user's store. The release preflight refuses a set `MEMINDEX_STORE`.
- The snapshot (`memindex_snapshot`, made by `scripts/eval-snapshot.ts`) is read-only by default. To
  bring its schema up to date, migrate it in one session:
  `MEMINDEX_STORE="…/memindex_snapshot?options=-c%20default_transaction_read_only%3Doff" memindex migrate`.
- Name scratch databases `memindex_<purpose>` and drop them when done.
- Check free disk (`df -h /`) before copying a database: keep at least 25 GB free.
- Workers and subagents never commit, stash, reset or checkout; the coordinating agent owns git.
